WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.239 --> 00:00:07.344
Diego Alvarez: Hey Frank, how's it going? How's the weather up in Tulsa today?

2
00:00:08.072 --> 00:00:14.409
Frank DeLuca: Not bad, not bad. A little chilly this morning, but the the sun's out. How about you?

3
00:00:15.655 --> 00:00:25.057
Diego Alvarez: Same here. I'm just trying to get through my coffee before the next call. So, I know we've got the renewal coming up in January.

4
00:00:25.057 --> 00:00:31.451
Diego Alvarez: Wanted to check in, see how things are going, and talk through any questions you might have.

5
00:00:32.077 --> 00:00:40.608
Frank DeLuca: Yeah, appreciate that. Things are mostly fine operationally. We're seeing decent call volume. Um, we're probably averaging around 11,000 calls a month across the seven rooftops.

6
00:00:40.608 --> 00:00:46.841
Frank DeLuca: The BDC team is at full strength now after we hired two new people in September. So that's helped.

7
00:00:47.583 --> 00:00:53.206
Diego Alvarez: Good to hear. And the Google Ads call conversions, still flowing through to Smart Bidding okay?

8
00:00:53.908 --> 00:01:03.769
Frank DeLuca: You know, yeah, that's fine. No issues there. Our marketing guy, uh, Nathan, he's been managing that. But look, I gotta be straight with you.

9
00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:07.319
Frank DeLuca: The renewal is not a slam dunk this time.

10
00:01:08.602 --> 00:01:10.300
Diego Alvarez: Okay, tell me more.

11
00:01:10.788 --> 00:01:27.607
Frank DeLuca: So, um, you know I came in August. New GM. I'm looking at all our vendor spend, and my boss, the regional VP, is asking me point blank whether we should renew with Invoca or take a hard look at Marchex.

12
00:01:27.607 --> 00:01:33.350
Frank DeLuca: And I'll be honest, the thing that keeps coming up is the billing structure.

13
00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:36.150
Diego Alvarez: The billing structure how?

14
00:01:36.837 --> 00:01:45.800
Frank DeLuca: Finance and procurement, they push back on paying separately for every little thing. You know, PreSense, QM seats, AI Voice Agent minutes.

15
00:01:45.800 --> 00:02:02.095
Frank DeLuca: And then Signal AI, we're paying for that as an add-on on top of call tracking. So when they see the renewal invoice, it's like, wait, we're already paying for call tracking, why is this other line item so big?

16
00:02:02.095 --> 00:02:03.317
Frank DeLuca: It creates friction.

17
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:11.064
Diego Alvarez: Got it. You know, so um, it's not necessarily the total number, it's the way it's broken out?

18
00:02:12.525 --> 00:02:26.034
Frank DeLuca: Yeah, I think that's fair. It's the add-on pricing friction at renewal. That's what I keep hearing. And honestly, when my boss asks me, 'Are we getting enough value to justify all these separate charges?', I don't have a great answer.

19
00:02:26.034 --> 00:02:32.954
Frank DeLuca: Like, I mean, we use Signal AI, but it's another line item. So yeah, it's a real question mark for us.

20
00:02:34.066 --> 00:02:46.255
Diego Alvarez: Okay. That's helpful to hear. Let me, uh, I can take that back to our team. I don't want to promise anything on the the call, but I can see what options might be available.

21
00:02:46.255 --> 00:02:54.264
Diego Alvarez: Can you tell me a little more about how your boss is framing it? Is it purely cost, or is there something else?

22
00:02:54.495 --> 00:03:02.116
Frank DeLuca: Mostly cost. I mean, he's not saying the product is bad. He's just saying, you know, we need to tighten up.

23
00:03:02.116 --> 00:03:09.737
Frank DeLuca: And when he sees all these separate charges, it makes him wonder if we're overpaying. So, so it's a real risk.

24
00:03:09.737 --> 00:03:15.906
Frank DeLuca: I'm not gonna lie, if we can't get comfortable with the pricing structure, we might not renew.

25
00:03:16.718 --> 00:03:24.431
Diego Alvarez: Understood. I'll bring that back. Let me ask, is there anything else that's coming up? Any other concerns?

26
00:03:24.694 --> 00:03:34.049
Frank DeLuca: No, I mean, uh, everything else is fine. The BDC team uses it every day. No complaints there. Just the billing thing.

27
00:03:34.393 --> 00:03:46.305
Diego Alvarez: Okay. So let me, uh, I'll talk to my manager and see what we can do. I can't promise anything, but I'll come back to you with something concrete.

28
00:03:46.305 --> 00:03:47.948
Diego Alvarez: Um, How's that sound?

29
00:03:48.836 --> 00:03:51.136
Frank DeLuca: That sounds good. I appreciate it.

30
00:03:51.571 --> 00:04:02.975
Diego Alvarez: Great. And, uh, I mean, just like, so I have it, are you still the main point of contact for the renewal, or should I loop in someone from finance?

31
00:04:04.299 --> 00:04:12.577
Frank DeLuca: You can keep me as the main contact. I'll handle finance. You know, just, you know, keep me in the loop.

32
00:04:12.995 --> 00:04:18.724
Diego Alvarez: Will do. And hey, how's the new GM role treating you? Settling in okay?

33
00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:30.093
Frank DeLuca: It's busy. A lot of moving parts. But it's good. I like the team here. We're just trying to get our processes tightened up.

34
00:04:30.671 --> 00:04:38.958
Diego Alvarez: I hear that. Well, let me get on this pricing thing and I'll follow up with you by early next week.

35
00:04:38.958 --> 00:04:40.142
Diego Alvarez: Does that work?

36
00:04:40.437 --> 00:04:42.618
Frank DeLuca: Um, yeah, that works. Thanks, Diego.

37
00:04:43.945 --> 00:04:46.145
Diego Alvarez: No problem. Uh, Talk soon.

38
00:04:47.522 --> 00:04:48.330
Frank DeLuca: Take care.
